# Solidity / Foundry Rules

## Post-Edit Checklist (MANDATORY)
After ANY edit to `.sol` files:
1. Run `cd packages/contracts && forge fmt` — auto-format all Solidity files
2. Run `npm run ci:contracts` from the repo root — runs `forge fmt --check` + `forge test` (the contracts-specific shard of CI). This is required because `npm run ci` deliberately excludes the contracts workspace to keep iteration fast for non-Solidity changes; only `.sol` edits need to pay the full Foundry suite cost.
3. If your changeset also touches non-Solidity code (TypeScript, CSS, configs, etc.), run `npm run ci` as well so the JS/TS lint + typecheck + test + build is also covered. Equivalently, `npm run ci:full` does both in one shot.

Do NOT skip these steps. Do NOT leave formatting or CI failures for the user to fix. Conversely, do NOT run `npm run ci:contracts` (or `ci:full`) when your changeset doesn't touch `.sol` files — the Foundry suite is the slowest thing in CI and re-running it for unrelated edits wastes minutes per turn.

## Style
- Use Solidity 0.8.x with the latest stable compiler
- Follow the Solidity style guide: contract-level NatSpec on all public/external functions
- Use `forge fmt` formatting (do not fight it)
- Errors must be custom errors (not `require` strings) for gas efficiency
- Events for all state mutations
- Use OpenZeppelin contracts from `lib/` (git submodules)

## Public-Facing Source — No Internal References (MANDATORY)

`packages/contracts/src/**/*.sol` is the only part of the repo that ships publicly (audit reports, Etherscan verification, third-party reviewers). Treat every comment as something an external reader will see with NO access to the rest of the repo.

**NEVER reference these from `src/` Solidity files:**
- Internal markdown docs: `AGENTS.md`, `docs/*.md`, `TODO.md`, `README.md` (anywhere in the repo).
- Internal repo paths: `apps/...`, `packages/<anything>/src/...`, `packages/<anything>/test/...`, `packages/<anything>/script/...`, `packages/shared/...`, `.cursor/...`, `.github/...`.
- Sibling-package source files by path: `packages/shared/src/vanity.ts`, `apps/web/src/...`, etc.
- GitHub issue/PR numbers (`issue #269`, `PR #343`, `(see #310)`) — the issue tracker is private.
- Internal repo URLs: `github.com/<our-org>/...`, `linear.app/...`, internal Notion / Slack links.
- Repo-internal task management language: "see TODO.md", "tracked in Linear", etc.

**OK to reference:**
- Other `.sol` files in `packages/contracts/src/` by contract / function / library name (e.g. `VanityMining.sol`, `Bonding._enterGraduating`, `Pair.swap`). These ship together.
- External public sources: BounceTech / OpenZeppelin / Foundry GitHub URLs, EIP numbers, Hyperliquid public docs.
- Generic architecture roles: "the frontend", "the indexer", "the keeper Worker", "the off-chain miner". These describe operational context without leaking repo structure.
- Test file names within the same `packages/contracts/test/` tree are tolerated **only when the test asserts a load-bearing invariant the comment is invoking** (e.g. "the brick-resistance contract is enforced by `test/HostilePreSeed.t.sol`"). Default to NOT referencing them — auditors won't see the test file unless we share it separately.

**When you would have written an `AGENTS.md` cross-reference, instead:**
- Inline the relevant rationale in the natspec on the function / storage field itself, OR
- Trust the contract-level natspec (which orients readers to the load-bearing pieces) and stay silent.

**Same constraint applies to any string baked into bytecode:** error messages, `revert(reason)` strings, event arg defaults — never embed an internal path.

This rule applies only to `packages/contracts/src/`. The contracts package's own `AGENTS.md`, `test/`, `script/`, and other sibling files are free to reference whatever they like — they don't ship.

**Audit your changes:** before declaring a `.sol` edit done, grep the modified file(s) for `AGENTS`, `docs/`, `apps/`, `packages/[a-z]+/src`, `issue\s*#\d+`, `\.ts\b`, `TODO\.md`. Any hit in `src/` is a defect to fix in the same edit.

## Security Checklist
Before any PR, verify:
- Reentrancy guards on external calls that transfer value
- Access control on admin functions (Ownable or role-based)
- Slippage protection on all swap/liquidity operations
- No floating pragma — pin exact compiler version
- Check-effects-interactions pattern
- Integer overflow is handled (Solidity 0.8+ default, but verify for unchecked blocks)

## Testing
- Write tests in Solidity (not JavaScript) using `forge test`
- Use `forge test --fork-url` for integration tests against live state
- Fuzz tests for math-heavy functions (bonding curve calculations)
- Invariant tests for protocol-level properties
- Name test files `*.t.sol`, place in `test/`
- Name test functions `test_<description>` for passing, `testFail_<description>` for expected reverts, `testFuzz_<description>` for fuzz tests

## Deployment (MANDATORY)
- Use `forge script` (not `forge create`) for reproducible deployments
- Scripts go in `script/`, named `Deploy<Contract>.s.sol`
- Never hardcode private keys — use `cast wallet import` encrypted keystores
- **Redeploy when contracts change:** Whenever `.sol` source files in `src/` are modified, the contracts MUST be redeployed so on-chain bytecode matches the repo. The deployed contracts must always match the source code.
- **HyperEVM big blocks (read this — fresh deploys WILL fail otherwise):** HyperEVM uses dual-block dispatch. Small blocks (~2M gas, ~1s) are the default; deploys exceed 2M gas and only fit in big blocks (~30M gas, ~60s). The setting is **per-wallet, persists**, and lives on the Hyperliquid L1 (NOT EVM) — `cast send` cannot toggle it. Use the helper:
  ```bash
  node scripts/toggle-big-blocks.mjs status   # check current state for the deployer
  node scripts/toggle-big-blocks.mjs on       # required before broadcasting Deploy.s.sol
  node scripts/toggle-big-blocks.mjs off      # optional, restore 1s confirms after deploy
  ```
  Symptom if you skip this: forge fails with `error code -32603: exceeds block gas limit` on the first deploy tx.
- **`--slow` is mandatory** for `Deploy.s.sol` because subsequent txs depend on prior contract state (factory.setRouter, role grants, addRouter, addDepositor). Without it forge will hit nonce/state mismatches.
- **Expect 15–20 minutes** for a full deploy with big blocks on (~14–19 sequential txs × ~60s).
- **Deployment steps:**
  1. Run tests: `forge test`
  2. Enable big blocks (one-time per wallet): `node scripts/toggle-big-blocks.mjs on`
  3. `forge clean && forge build` (avoid stale artifacts after rename/refactor commits)
  4. Deploy: `source .env && forge script script/Deploy.s.sol:Deploy --rpc-url "$HYPEREVM_RPC_URL" --broadcast --slow`
  5. Export ABIs: `npm run export-abi --workspace @launchpad/contracts`
  6. Update addresses in `packages/shared/src/constants/addresses.ts` with new proxy/contract addresses
  7. Update `BONDING_START_BLOCK` in `packages/shared/src/constants/chains.ts` to the **lowest** receipt block from `broadcast/Deploy.s.sol/999/run-latest.json`
  8. Update hardcoded `DEFAULT_BONDING` / `DEFAULT_ZAP` addresses in `packages/contracts/script/E2ETest.s.sol`
  9. Rebuild shared so consumers see new addresses: `npm run build --workspace @launchpad/shared`
  10. Run `npm run ci:full` from repo root to verify everything compiles (deploys touch both Solidity and the shared/typed-address surface, so the full sweep is appropriate here)
  11. Sanity-check on-chain wiring (`Bonding.tokenImplementation`, `Bonding.factory`, `Bonding.router`, `Bonding.isRouter(zap)`, `Zap.bonding`, `Factory.router`) — see [`packages/contracts/AGENTS.md`](mdc:packages/contracts/AGENTS.md#post-deploy-sanity-checks).
